Implements the two builds from the 2026-08-28 context/frame design note and
its appended independent-review correction, in order.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6740: _goal_only_prompt rendered previous_level_complete_grid
through to_ascii -- the last full-grid ASCII render in the induce-prompt
family. Now _rle_grid plus a two-sentence encoding explanation. Lossless.
Measured with the pinned Qwen3.8-27B GGUF tokenizer on real reset frames:
tu93 goal prompt 4,309 -> 1,928 tokens (-2,381); ft09 4,309 -> 2,995
(-1,314). The saving is game-shaped, per the correction's 8-game sweep.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6730: CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_TOOL_LOOP=selfparse runs the induction
tool loop with agent-side transport: NO tools request field (the scored
vLLM server 400s on one), schemas as prompt text rendered from TOOL_SCHEMAS,
the model's Qwen3-coder XML parsed by the loop (post-</think> only,
schema-typed coercion, truncated blocks counted never dispatched), results
fed back as user-side <tool_response> blocks. "", "1", "repair" stay
byte-identical. Pre-registered transport gate PASSED at ceiling on the
local CUDA backend: 20/20 first-turn attempts (>=80% required), 20/20
parse-to-dispatch (>=95% required), 0 dispatch failures, 5 games x 4 seeds.
Scope: all 20 live calls were zero-arg list_transitions; the code-carrying
shape is covered by the stored vLLM emission (parsed 1/1) and unit fixtures.

NOT built, deliberately: fetch-on-demand object table (correction withdrew
it -- the 4,667 tokens are bought by a measured held-out change_fidelity
win, p=0.0192); the scored kernel keeps repair mode until the resumed
holdout-equalized A/B answers quality under selfparse.

Rejected while building: a stop-string on </tool_call> (fires inside inline
think text on backends that do not split reasoning_content).

12 new tests (SCENARIO-ARC-WMTE-6731..6741); 8 mutations each RED then
restored byte-identical; 120 tool-loop-family tests green; ruff+mypy clean.

